---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SandhiPad from "../../islands/SandhiPad.tsx";
---
<Base title="Sandhi" kind="tool" description="Join two Sanskrit words and see which Pāṇinian sūtras decide what happens where they meet: vowel sandhi (6.1.77–6.1.128) and consonant sandhi (6.1.73–8.4.65), with every optional form.">
  <div class="page-narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/tools/">Tools</a></p>
      <h1>Sandhi</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Join two words. Where two vowels meet, the tool tests every vowel rule of the Aṣṭādhyāyī, shows which one wins and
        why the others step aside. Where a consonant is involved, it runs the consonant rules in the order the grammar
        prescribes. Either way you get the derivation sūtra by sūtra and every other correct form.
        Taught in <a href="/course/ac-sandhi/yan/">Vowel sandhi</a> and <a href="/course/hal-sandhi/scutva/">Consonant sandhi</a>.
      </p>
    </header>
    <SandhiPad client:load syncUrl />
  </div>
</Base>
